/-- 7:D5 — **no definite space**: for every prime shell `p`, every `ν` and any three vectors `u, v, w` of `𝔽_p⁴`, some
nonzero coefficient triple gives a null vector of the determinant form `x₀² − x₁² − x₃² + ν x₂²` in their span —
every three-dimensional subspace of the register square contains a null vector (`FRC.Lorentz.isotropic_three`,
`Theme/Lorentz.lean`, by Chevalley–Warning). -/
theorem isotropic_three {p : ℕ} [Fact p.Prime] (ν : ZMod p) (u v w : Fin 4 → ZMod p) :
    ∃ a : Fin 3 → ZMod p, a ≠ 0 ∧ FRC.Lorentz.Qf ν (a 0 • u + a 1 • v + a 2 • w) = 0 :=
  FRC.Lorentz.isotropic_three ν u v w

